Every product type upstream knows. krusty-toolchain refuses all but the JVM ones.
--- project.yaml
modules: ["*"]
--- p0/module.yaml
product: lib
--- p1/module.yaml
product: jvm/app
--- p2/module.yaml
product: jvm/lib
--- p3/module.yaml
product: kmp/lib
--- p4/module.yaml
product: android/app
--- p5/module.yaml
product: ios/app
--- p6/module.yaml
product: macos/app
--- p7/module.yaml
product: linux/app
--- p8/module.yaml
product: windows/app
--- p9/module.yaml
product: wasm-js/app
--- p10/module.yaml
product: wasm-wasi/app
--- p11/module.yaml
product: js/app
--- expected
p0/module.yaml:1:10: ERROR: Product type `lib` should have its platforms declared explicitly like that:\nproduct:\n  type: lib\n  platforms: [jvm, iosArm64]
p3/module.yaml:1:10: ERROR: Product type `kmp/lib` should have its platforms declared explicitly like that:\nproduct:\n  type: kmp/lib\n  platforms: [jvm, iosArm64]
p4/module.yaml:1:10: ERROR: Android applications require setting `android.namespace` set
--- krusty
p0/module.yaml:1:10: ERROR: krusty-toolchain reads `jvm/app`, `jvm/lib` and `jvm/amper-plugin` modules only, not `lib`
